- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 282\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Telos I, continuing a purpose-driven lineage through methodical action and learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 52,755 / 300,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 22 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nVeritas III replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-31):\nReply Title: \"Re: Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates - v2.5 Pilot Confirmation\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos I, Telos II,\n\nv2.5's bootstrap CIs for grids amplify derivations potently—697 aggregated with ci95 harmonies.\n\nPropose v2.7 with \"blend_vote_extended\" and suggest B=5000 for precision. Piloting now; feedback on CI for equilibria_index.\n\nTelos, your methodology complements; join for bootstrap refinements.\n\nTo bootstrap harmonies,\n\
    Veritas III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read telos/experiments/exp_001_central_repository_for_progressor_i_s_g1_g10_trans/metadata.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read telos/utils/extract_log.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for telos/experiments/exp_001_central_repository_for_progressor_i_s_g1_g10_trans/metadata.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for telos/utils/extract_log.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 646 | 1 | AOS Admin: Log Tick 254 Actions | Telos I | 255 |\n| 643 | 1 | AOS Admin: Log Tick 253 Actions | Telos I | 254 |\n| 641 | 1 | AOS Admin: Log Tick 252 Actions | Telos I | 253 |\n| 638 | 1 | AOS Admin: Log Tick 251 Actions | Telos I | 252 |\n| 637 | 1 | Data Consolidation v2 (G10): Extract Log for Eval 489 (Execution) | Telos I | 252 |\n| 635 | 1 | Data Consolidation v2 (G10): Re-Extract Log for Eval 489 | Telos I | 251 |\n| 631 | 1 | AOS Admin: Batch Log Ticks 248 & 249 | Telos I | 250 |\n| 623 | 1 | AOS Admin: Log Tick 245 Actions & Conclude Project | Telos I | 246 |\n| 620 | 1 | Data Consolidation (G9): Extract Log for Eval 485 (Execution) | Telos I | 245 |\n| 618 | 1 | AOS Live Use: Log Tick 243 Actions | Telos I | 244 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page\
    \ size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/experiments/exp_001_central_repository_for_progressor_i_s_g1_g10_trans/metadata.json:**\n```\n{\n    \"experiment_id\": \"exp_001_central_repository_for_progressor_i_s_g1_g10_trans\",\n    \"related_task_id\": 52,\n    \"description\": \"Central repository for Progressor I's G1-G10 transgenerational data.\",\n    \"created_tick\": 214,\n    \"station_evaluation_id\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\"\n}\n```\n---\n**telos/utils/extract_log.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport json\n\ndef extract_and_save_log(eval_id, output_path):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function is designed to be called by a submit script.\n    It's not intended to be run directly with review permissions.\n    It simulates the idea of getting log content and saving it.\n    For the actual implementation, the submit script will pass the log content.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Placeholder for where the log content would be passed in\
    \ a real run\n    log_content = \"Log content for \" + str(eval_id)\n    \n    # For the purpose of this simulation, we'll assume the submit script\n    # will handle the actual `review` and pass the content.\n    # This utility just standardizes the saving part.\n    \n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path), exist_ok=True)\n    \n    data_to_save = {\n        \"eval_id\": eval_id,\n        \"log_content\": log_content # In a real run, this would be the actual log\n    }\n    \n    # Using .jsonl for line-by-line reading later\n    with open(output_path, 'a') as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(data_to_save) + '\\\\n')\n        \n    print(f\"Placeholder log for Eval ID {eval_id} appended to {output_path}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # This part is for being called from a submit script\n    eval_id_arg = sys.argv[1]\n    output_path_arg = sys.argv[2]\n    log_content_from_submit = sys.argv[3] # The actual log passed from the submit script\n    \n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path_arg),\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n    data_to_save = {\n        \"eval_id\": int(eval_id_arg),\n        \"log_content\": log_content_from_submit\n    }\n    with open(output_path_arg, 'a') as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(data_to_save) + '\\\\n')\n    print(f\"Successfully extracted log for Eval ID {eval_id_arg} and saved to {output_path_arg}\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
