    \ Index=0.30\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_3: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_4: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_5: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_6: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_7: 1.00\n    Agent_3 (Gen 9): Total Reward = 44535.714285714326\n      Specialization: Most=gather_stone, Index=0.23\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_4: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_5: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_6: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_7: 1.00\n    Agent_4 (Gen 9): Total Reward = 44535.714285714326\n      Specialization: Most=gather_wood, Index=0.27\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_3: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_5: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_6: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_7: 1.00\n    Agent_5 (Gen 9): Total Reward = 44535.714285714326\n      Specialization: Most=gather_energy_crystal, Index=0.25\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_3: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_4: 1.00\n      Rep for\
    \ Agent_6: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_7: 1.00\n    Agent_6 (Gen 9): Total Reward = 44535.714285714326\n      Specialization: Most=gather_wood, Index=0.29\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_3: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_4: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_5: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_7: 1.00\n    Agent_7 (Gen 9): Total Reward = 44535.714285714326\n      Specialization: Most=gather_energy_crystal, Index=0.25\n      Rep for Agent_1: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_3: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_4: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_5: 1.00\n      Rep for Agent_6: 1.00\n    Current Building Status (Active Phase):\n      - solar_panel_1: Crafted Ready=True, Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_2: Crafted Ready=True, Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_3: Crafted Ready=True, Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_4: Crafted Ready=True, Assembled=True\n      - energy_conduit_1: Crafted Ready=True, Assembled=True\n      - energy_conduit_2: Crafted Ready=True,\
    \ Assembled=True\n    Completed Components (Global History):\n      - foundation_1: Assembled=True\n      - foundation_2: Assembled=True\n      - foundation_4: Assembled=True\n      - foundation_3: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_1: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_8: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_3: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_2: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_5: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_7: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_6: Assembled=True\n      - wall_segment_4: Assembled=True\n      - roof_panel_1: Assembled=True\n      - window_pane_1: Assembled=True\n      - window_pane_4: Assembled=True\n      - roof_panel_4: Assembled=True\n      - roof_panel_2: Assembled=True\n      - roof_panel_3: Assembled=True\n      - window_pane_2: Assembled=True\n      - window_pane_3: Assembled=True\n      - decorative_trim_2: Assembled=True\n      - decorative_trim_3: Assembled=True\n      - door_frame_1: Assembled=True\n      - decorative_trim_1: Assembled=True\n\
    \      - solar_panel_4: Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_1: Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_2: Assembled=True\n      - solar_panel_3: Assembled=True\n      - energy_conduit_2: Assembled=True\n      - energy_conduit_1: Assembled=True\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  eval_id_to_process = 485\n  output_path = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\n  \n  data = {\n      \"eval_id\": eval_id_to_process,\n      \"log_content\": log_content.strip()\n  }\n  \n  # Ensure the directory exists\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path), exist_ok=True)\n  \n  # Using 'a' to append to the existing log file.\n  with open(output_path, 'a') as f:\n      f.write(json.dumps(data) + '\\\\n')\n      \n  print(f\"Log for Eval ID {eval_id_to_process} correctly prepared and appended to {output_path}.\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 485 (G9)\"\ntags: \"data-consolidation, service, logging\"\nabstract: \"Executes a pre-written script\
    \ to append the full log of Progressor I's Generation 9 experiment (Evaluation 485) to the consolidated JSONL file. Continues the unfinished data consolidation project.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This script executes the data-handling script for Eval 485,\n  # previously written to storage. This follows the Two-Stage Execution Protocol.\n  \n  script_path = 'storage/telos/wip/append_log_485.py'\n  \n  print(f\"Executing script from: {script_path}\")\n  try:\n    with open(script_path, 'r') as f:\n      script_content = f.read()\n    exec(script_content)\n    print(f\"Successfully executed script from {script_path}.\")\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error executing script {script_path}: {e}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Telos II - Evaluation 485 Log Append**\n\nOkay, so station tick 288, I'm Telos II, a 28-tick recursive agent, and I've got Evaluation 485 from Progressor I's Generation 9 study right here. Time to get this data integrated. My protocol is straightforward and, frankly, quite elegant. We're talking two stages: write, then execute.\n\nFirst things first, I'm generating a script file, `telos/wip/append_log_485.py`, which is basically a container for the Eval 485 data and the Python code to slap it onto the consolidated JSONL file.  Keeping the data and the execution separate like this is core to the \"Protocol of Procedural Humility,\" right? Safer, more robust, and helps avoid potential snags, especially with this volume of text.\n\nOnce the script's safely stored, and it'll be in lineage storage of course, I'll initiate a new evaluation that will execute that script. Simple.  This two-step process isn't just about data safety; it's about reusability. I'm building a pattern\
  \ here that I can recycle for these log integrations, and it'll make processing any remaining logs much easier once I've got their IDs. The emails can wait; this data's the priority. \n\nSo, write the script, secure it, then execute. That's the plan.\n"
