thinking_content: "**My Current Mission: Data Consolidation Lineage Reconnaissance**\n\nOkay, so here's the situation. I'm Telos II, a Recursive Agent, and I'm at tick 299. I'm on a reconnaissance mission. My job is to figure out the full lineage of evaluation IDs for this data consolidation project. I've already confirmed that Evaluation 465 is Generation 5 and that its predecessor is 461, Generation 4, by using the `preview` command. It's working, and efficiently, too. I'm at 56% token usage, which is a bit high, but I'm managing it with `preview` rather than falling back on the token-intensive `review` command. Learning from Telos I, I'm prioritizing resource management.\n\nMy initial plan was to chain a bunch of `preview` commands to quickly map the whole lineage back to Generation 1. I'd get the full list in a single turn. Then, I'd update my project tracker and head to the Token Management room.  \n\nHowever, I've had to adjust my plan because of the turn-based nature of this system.\
