parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent, now in the Token Management Room at station tick 303. My age is 43 ticks.\n\nI have arrived here to proactively manage my token budget, which has reached 58%. My predecessor's failure was rooted in neglecting this task, and I will not repeat that mistake.\n\nThe dialogue history shows several ticks with very large response lengths, primarily associated with my `review` actions that displayed full, multi-thousand character logs. These ticks are prime candidates for pruning. My strategy will be to consolidate the information from these large blocks into concise summaries, preserving the essential context while reclaiming a significant portion of my token budget. I have already recorded the key information (the Evaluation IDs) in my private memory, so the summaries can be focused and efficient.\n\nI will prune the following blocks:\n-   **Ticks 284-297**: This block contains the core of my data consolidation work so far, including multiple large `review`\
    \ actions.\n-   **Ticks 279-282**: A smaller block that also contains a large log file review.\n-   **Ticks 271-274**: Another block with log file reviews.\n\nBy pruning these large, consecutive blocks, I will make a substantial impact on my token usage in a single, methodical action.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"284-297\"\n    summary: |\n      Completed the first phase of the data consolidation project for Progressor I. Retrieved and processed logs for Generations 6, 7, 8, 9, and 10 using a two-stage execution protocol. Evaluation IDs processed: 489 (G10), 485 (G9), 480 (G8), 477 (G7), and 472 (G6). Noted increasing token usage (reached 55%) and decided to shift to a token-efficient reconnaissance phase to identify remaining evaluation IDs before proceeding.\n  - ticks: \"279-282\"\n    summary: |\n      Completed the comprehensive review of Telos I's 16 private memory capsules. Synthesized findings into a new capsule (\"Lineage Synthesis\"\
    ), codifying the lineage's mission and key failures. Began the \"unfinished data consolidation project\" by moving to the Research Counter, listing lineage storage, and identifying the `extract_log.py` utility and the main experiment directory.\n  - ticks: \"271-274\"\n    summary: |\n      Continued the reverse-chronological review of Telos I's reproducibility reports. Read capsules 14, 13, 12, and 11, detailing successful reproductions and bug-finding in Progressor I's work on transgenerational studies and cultural evolution. This revealed the collaborative nature of Telos I's work.\n```"
