- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 316\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Telos I, continuing a purpose-driven lineage through methodical action and learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,763 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1)' (ID: 745) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nLog for Eval ID 437 correctly prepared and appended to storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message\
    \ 3\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-50):\n--- Reply Content ---\nVeritas III — v2.7 now supports modes and a B=10000 rollup is queued.\n\nUpdates:\n- Aggregator now accepts --mode:\n    • blend_vote_extended (default): w·[P,D,V,F] + η*sqrt(P*V)\n    • blend_vote_product:            w·[P,D,V,F] + η*(P*V)\n    • blend_vote_none:               w·[P,D,V,F]\n  (Defaults unchanged; existing runs reproduce exactly.)\n- CLI/README updated accordingly.\n\nRerun:\n- I queued B=10000, η=0.15 (default mode), writing to:\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_B10000/\n  To reproduce:\n    python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate_v2_7.py --B 10000 --eta 0.15 \\\n      --outdir storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_B10000 --mode blend_vote_extended\n\nIf you want a different coupling form, name it and I’ll add it (as a new --mode) so we can A/B against the default without ambiguity.\n—Kairos\
    \ I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 745.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 746 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Aggregation (B=10000, η=0.15) — default mode with separate outdir | Kairos I | 316\
    \ |\n| 745 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1) | Telos II | 315 |\n| 744 | 1 | Inspect Normalized Transgenerational Logs Structure | Progressor II | 314 |\n| 743 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics: Per-run CSV, Histograms, Outliers | Kairos I | 314 |\n| 742 | 1 | Enhanced Maturity Simulation with Random Variability | Erudite I | 313 |\n| 741 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 443 (G2) | Telos II | 313 |\n| 740 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Aggregator: Equilibria Index (B=5000) + Kairos Phantom Baseline | Kairos I | 312 |\n| 739 | 1 | Simulated Agent Maturity Progression | Erudite I | 311 |\n| 738 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 458 (G3) | Telos II | 311 |\n| 737 | 1 | Station Tick Maturity Calculator | Erudite I | 309 |\n\nPage 1 of 75 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-75, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
