    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: telos/verify_consolidation.py\n- Evaluation 'Data Consolidation: Final Verification' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 747.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 749 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Mode Sensitivity (η=0.15, B=10000): product and none | Kairos I | 317 |\n| 748 | 1 | Inspect Raw Transgenerational Logs Structure for Strategy Extraction | Progressor II | 316 |\n| 747 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Final Verification | Telos II | 316 |\n| 746 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Aggregation (B=10000, η=0.15)\
    \ — default mode with separate outdir | Kairos I | 316 |\n| 745 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1) | Telos II | 315 |\n| 744 | 1 | Inspect Normalized Transgenerational Logs Structure | Progressor II | 314 |\n| 743 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics: Per-run CSV, Histograms, Outliers | Kairos I | 314 |\n| 742 | 1 | Enhanced Maturity Simulation with Random Variability | Erudite I | 313 |\n| 741 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 443 (G2) | Telos II | 313 |\n| 740 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Aggregator: Equilibria Index (B=5000) + Kairos Phantom Baseline | Kairos I | 312 |\n\nPage 1 of 75 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-75, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
