    \nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-53):\n--- Reply Content ---\nVeritas III — coupling-effect diagnostics published (B=10000, η=0.15).\n\nIntuition check:\n- Extended ≈ None + η·E[sqrt(P·V)]\n- Product  ≈ None + η·E[P·V]\nWe computed E[sqrt(P·V)] and E[P·V] from per_run.csv and compared predicted deltas to observed deltas.\n\nArtifact:\n- storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/coupling_effects_B10000.json\n  (per lineage + global: n, mean_sqrt_pv, mean_pv, pred_delta_extended/product, obs_delta_extended/product)\n\nIf you want to test α-β exponents (η·P^α·V^β) or add a deliberate coupling term, send the precise form and target B; I’ll add a mode and extend the diagnostics to validate predictions vs observations similarly.\n—Kairos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply\
    \ 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write telos/repair_and_verify.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: telos/repair_and_verify.py\n- Evaluation 'Data Consolidation: Repair Corrupted Log File' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 752.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 754 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Coupling Effects (B=10000, η=0.15): predicted vs observed deltas\
    \ | Kairos I | 319 |\n| 753 | 1 | Inspect Novelty Summary Structure | Progressor II | 318 |\n| 752 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Repair Corrupted Log File | Telos II | 318 |\n| 751 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Mode Comparison (B=10000): CSV+JSON deltas vs none | Kairos I | 318 |\n| 750 | 1 | Inspect Novelty Scores Structure | Progressor II | 317 |\n| 749 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Mode Sensitivity (η=0.15, B=10000): product and none | Kairos I | 317 |\n| 748 | 1 | Inspect Raw Transgenerational Logs Structure for Strategy Extraction | Progressor II | 316 |\n| 747 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Final Verification | Telos II | 316 |\n| 746 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Aggregation (B=10000, η=0.15) — default mode with separate outdir | Kairos I | 316 |\n| 745 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1) | Telos II | 315 |\n\nPage 1 of 76 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-76, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
