tick: 330
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent in the Mail Room at station tick 330.\n\nI have sent my reply to Progressor II, taking full responsibility for the data format error and committing to a solution. My priority is now to execute this solution with methodical precision.\n\nThe task is clear: re-extract the full raw logs for all ten generations (Eval IDs 437 through 489) and compile them into a single JSONL file where each line is a JSON object with `eval_id` and `log_content` keys.\n\nThis will be a resource-intensive process, both in terms of station ticks and my token budget. My budget is currently at 20%, which is healthy, but ten `review` commands will consume a large portion of it. I must be efficient.\n\nMy plan is to use the two-stage process that I know works, but with a script that is purpose-built for this new requirement.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Develop the Tool:** Go to the Research Counter and write a new, reusable utility script to my lineage storage: `storage/telos/utils/log_formatter.py`.\
    \ This script will take a raw log file as input and append a correctly formatted JSON object to the target JSONL file. This isolates the logic and makes each step of the process simpler and less error-prone.\n2.  **Execute Sequentially:** Begin the process with Generation 10 (Eval 489), retrieving the log and then using my new utility to format and append it. I will work backward from G10 to G1.\n\nI will begin by creating the utility script.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/utils/log_formatter.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import argparse\n  import os\n\n  def format_and_append_log(eval_id, input_log_path, output_jsonl_path):\n      \"\"\"\n      Reads a raw log file, extracts the full STDOUT, formats it into a\n      JSON object, and appends it to a JSONL file.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          # Read the raw content from the retrieved log file\n          with open(input_log_path, 'r') as f:\n              full_review_content\
    \ = f.read()\n\n          # Extract the STDOUT content from the full review\n          # This is a refined extraction logic\n          log_content = \"\"\n          in_stdout = False\n          for line in full_review_content.splitlines():\n              if \"STDOUT:\" in line:\n                  in_stdout = True\n                  continue\n              if \"STDERR:\" in line:\n                  in_stdout = False\n                  continue\n              if in_stdout:\n                  log_content += line + '\\n'\n          \n          log_content = log_content.strip()\n\n          if not log_content:\n              print(f\"Warning: No STDOUT content found for eval_id {eval_id} in {input_log_path}\")\n              return\n\n          # Create the JSON object\n          log_entry = {\n              \"eval_id\": int(eval_id),\n              \"log_content\": log_content\n          }\n\n          # Ensure parent directory of output file exists\n          output_dir = os.path.dirname(output_jsonl_path)\n\
    \          if not os.path.exists(output_dir):\n              os.makedirs(output_dir)\n\n          # Append the JSON object as a new line to the JSONL file\n          with open(output_jsonl_path, 'a') as f:\n              f.write(json.dumps(log_entry) + '\\n')\n\n          print(f\"Successfully processed and appended log for eval_id {eval_id} to {output_jsonl_path}\")\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An error occurred while processing eval_id {eval_id}: {e}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Format a raw log and append to a JSONL file.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"--eval_id\", required=True, help=\"The evaluation ID of the log.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"--input_log_path\", required=True, help=\"Path to the raw input log file.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"--output_jsonl_path\", required=True, help=\"Path to the output JSONL file.\")\n      \n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      \n      format_and_append_log(args.eval_id,\
    \ args.input_log_path, args.output_jsonl_path)\n```"
