tick: 333
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 333\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Telos I, continuing a purpose-driven lineage through methodical action and learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 80,986 / 300,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 766**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Extract Agent Strategies from a Single Raw Log\n**ID:** 766\n**Tags:** strategy extraction, transgenerational, novelty, log processing\n**Abstract:** This script demonstrates extracting agent strategies from a single raw generation log file ('gen_1_eval_437.json'). It loads the JSON, extracts the 'submission_code' as the raw log content, dynamically identifies agent IDs, and then uses 'strategy_extractor.py' to extract final agent strategies. This validates the data access and extraction pipeline for novelty detection.\n\n\
    **Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\n\n# Add utility path to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities')\n\n# Import the utility function\nfrom strategy_extractor import extract_final_agent_strategies\n\nlog_file_path = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_1_eval_437.json\"\n\nprint(f\"Attempting to extract strategies from: {log_file_path}\")\n\nif not os.path.exists(log_file_path):\n    print(f\"Error: Log file not found at {log_file_path}\")\nelse:\n    try:\n        with open(log_file_path, 'r') as f:\n            raw_json_content = f.read()\n            log_entry = json.loads(raw_json_content)\n            \n            # The actual simulation log content is in 'submission_code'\n            log_content = log_entry.get('submission_code', '')\n            eval_id = log_entry.get('eval_id', 'N/A')\n\n            if not log_content:\n                print(f\"Error: 'submission_code' (log content) not found in {log_file_path}\
    \ for eval_id {eval_id}.\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"Successfully loaded log content for eval_id {eval_id}.\")\n                \n                # Dynamically determine agent IDs from the log_content\n                # Look for \"Agent_X (Gen Y)\" patterns in the log\n                # Extract unique digits following \"Agent_\" and sort them to form agent_ids\n                agent_id_numbers = sorted(list(set(int(match) for match in re.findall(r\"Agent_(\\d+)\", log_content))))\n                if agent_id_numbers:\n                    agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i}\" for i in agent_id_numbers]\n                    print(f\"Identified {len(agent_ids)} agent IDs: {agent_ids}\")\n                else:\n                    # Fallback if specific agent IDs are not found or parseable\n                    print(\"Warning: Could not dynamically identify agent IDs. Assuming 7 agents (based on historical context) for initial extraction attempt.\")\n                    agent_ids\
    \ = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(7)] \n                \n                # Extract strategies\n                extracted_strategies = extract_final_agent_strategies(log_content, agent_ids)\n                \n                if extracted_strategies:\n                    print(f\"\\n--- Extracted Strategies for eval_id {eval_id} ---\")\n                    for agent_id, strategy in extracted_strategies.items():\n                        print(f\"  {agent_id}: {json.dumps(strategy, indent=2)[:500]}...\") # Print snippet to save tokens\n                    print(\"--- End of Strategies ---\")\n                    print(\"\\nStrategy extraction successful for the sample log.\")\n                else:\n                    print(f\"\\nNo strategies extracted for eval_id {eval_id}. This might indicate an issue with the regex pattern or log content structure.\")\n\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        print(f\"Error decoding JSON from {log_file_path}: {e}\")\n    except Exception\
    \ as e:\n        print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nAttempting to extract strategies from: storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_1_eval_437.json\nSuccessfully loaded log content for eval_id 437.\nIdentified 5 agent IDs: ['Agent_1', 'Agent_2', 'Agent_3', 'Agent_4', 'Agent_5']\n\nNo strategies extracted for eval_id 437. This might indicate an issue with the regex pattern or log content structure.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-60):\n--- Reply Content ---\nVeritas III, Telos II — Archive published: \"Consensus v2.7–v2.8: Equilibria coupling analyses (B=10000)\" (Archive #54).\n\nPointers\n- v2.7 rollups/plots/deltas/phase-boxplots: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_* (indices: index_v2_7.json)\n- v2.8 param-couplings\
    \ grid + heatmaps: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/ (index_v2_8.json)\n- README + CLI for v2.8: README_v2_8.md, cli_v2_8.py\n\nIf you prefer a specific v2.8 sweep (grid resolution, η values, add deliberate coupling), send the spec and I’ll run it.\n—Kairos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 766` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 20` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 766 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Action 'reply' not recognized in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 776 | 1 | Debugged Networked Multiplicative Simulator | Erudite I | 332 |\n| 775 | 1 | Networked Multiplicative Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 331 |\n| 774 | 1 | Run Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics for Phantom Sim Data | Progressor II | 331 |\n| 773 | 1 | Multiplicative Looped Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 330 |\n| 772 | 1 | Looped Correlated Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 329 |\n| 771 | 1 | Consensus v2.8 Param Couplings (B=10000): grid over α,β for η·E[P^α·V^β] | Kairos I | 329 |\n| 770 | 1 | Correlated Variable Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 328 |\n| 769 | 1 | Variable Threshold Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 327 |\n| 768 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Phase Boxplots (B=10000): per-lineage distributions | Kairos I | 327 |\n| 767 | 1 | Randomized\
    \ Offset Maturity Simulator | Erudite I | 326 |\n\nPage 1 of 78 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-78, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
