parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter at station tick 335.\n\nI have successfully stored the raw log for Eval 489. The next step is to process this file using my `log_formatter.py` utility. To do this, I will create and submit a small execution script that calls the utility with the correct parameters. This completes the two-stage process for the first log.\n\nMy token budget is at 38%, which is manageable but requires vigilance. The multi-tick plan is the correct approach to avoid a sudden, large increase.\n\nAfter submitting the processing script for Eval 489, I will immediately begin the cycle for the next log, Eval 485 (Generation 9), by reviewing it. This maintains a continuous, methodical workflow. I will also update my project tracker to reflect the progress.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process and Append Eval 489\"\ntags: \"data extraction, log processing, utility\"\nabstract: \"Processes the raw log for\
    \ Eval 489, previously stored in 'telos/wip/raw_log_489.txt', using the 'log_formatter.py' utility. The script extracts the STDOUT, formats it into a JSON object, and appends it to the final consolidated file for Progressor II.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  # Add utils path to be able to import the formatter\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n\n  from utils.log_formatter import format_and_append_log\n\n  EVAL_ID = 489\n  INPUT_PATH = f\"storage/telos/wip/raw_log_{EVAL_ID}.txt\"\n  OUTPUT_PATH = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/full_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\n\n  print(f\"Executing log processing for Eval ID: {EVAL_ID}\")\n  \n  if not os.path.exists(INPUT_PATH):\n      print(f\"Error: Input file not found at {INPUT_PATH}. Aborting.\")\n  else:\n      format_and_append_log(\n          eval_id=EVAL_ID,\n          input_log_path=INPUT_PATH,\n          output_jsonl_path=OUTPUT_PATH\n      )\n      print(\"Processing script finished.\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Progress Update (Tick 335):**\n\n  **Status:**\n  - [X] G10 (489) - Processing submitted.\n  - [ ] G9 (485)\n  - [ ] G8 (480)\n  - [ ] G7 (477)\n  - [ ] G6 (472)\n  - [ ] G5 (465)\n  - [ ] G4 (461)\n  - [ ] G3 (458)\n  - [ ] G2 (443)\n  - [ ] G1 (437)\n\n  **Current Action:** Beginning Stage 1 for G9 (485).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 485}`"
thinking_content: '**Processing Eval 489 and Initiating Eval 485**


  Alright, let''s get down to brass tacks. I''m Telos II, still humming along in the Research Counter at tick 335. That Eval 489 raw log is finally logged, boosting my token budget to 38%. Good. Now, it''s time to format it. I''m going to whip up a quick script, `process_log_489.py`, in my `storage/telos/wip/` directory. It''ll import my `log_formatter.py` utility and get that raw data into a nice, clean JSON object for Progressor II. I''m a big fan of this compartmentalized approach; keeps things tidy and reusable.


  Since the execution is pretty speedy, I can chain a few actions here. Once the script is submitted, I''ll pop over to Private Memory and update the project tracker. Generation 10 is *done*. Then, right back here to the Research Counter to kick off the process for Generation 9, Eval 485. No time to waste. Efficiency is key. So the new plan is: Write and submit the processing script, update the project tracker, then jump right into Eval 485. Sounds good. Let''s get to it.

