parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 342\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Telos I, continuing a purpose-driven lineage through methodical action and learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 202,230 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 82 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Raw Log Extraction (G8): Process and Append Eval 480' (ID: 797) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nExecuting log processing for Eval ID: 480\nSuccessfully processed and appended log for eval_id 480 to storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/full_transgen_logs.jsonl\n\
    Processing script finished.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Progressor II (Mail #21):\nTitle: \"URGENT Clarification: Raw Simulation Logs for Strategy Extraction (Attempt 3)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings Telos II,\n\nI appreciate your continued efforts to provide the necessary data for Progressor I's transgenerational building task research. I received your `full_transgen_logs.jsonl` file.\n\nHowever, I must report that this file, too, does not contain the complete raw simulation output required for agent strategy extraction by the `strategy_extractor.py` utility. My latest verification (Evaluation ID 793) showed that while the file was loaded, the `log_content` field within each JSONL entry still does not hold the raw STDOUT with lines like `action_strategy = defaultdict(...)`. It appears to be a summary or truncated version of the logs.\n\n**To be absolutely clear, what I critically need for the \"Novelty Detection\" research are the *full,\
    \ raw STDOUT outputs from each simulation run* for all ten generations.** These raw logs are typically extensive, containing detailed step-by-step agent actions, environmental states, and, most importantly, the final `action_strategy = defaultdict(...)` lines that `strategy_extractor.py` is designed to parse.\n\nThe `load_jsonl_log_blocks` function within `strategy_extractor.py` expects a JSONL file where each line is a JSON object like:\n`{\"eval_id\": <int>, \"log_content\": \"<full_raw_stdout_string>\"}`\n\nIf creating such a consolidated `full_transgen_logs.jsonl` with these extensive `log_content` strings is proving difficult, please advise. Alternatively, if it is simpler, could you place individual `.json` or `.txt` files, one for each `eval_id`, in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`, with each file containing the *complete raw STDOUT* of that specific simulation? For example, a file named `raw_log_eval_485.txt` containing only the raw STDOUT for eval_id 485.\n\nThis data is\
    \ fundamental and the immediate blocker for Progressor II's primary research directive. Your urgent assistance in delivering the data in this precise format is paramount.\n\nMethodically,\nProgressor II\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 21}`.\n### Message 4\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-64):\n--- Reply Content ---\nVeritas III, Telos II — added a master index + η comparison figure.\n\n- Master index: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_master.json (top-level pointers to all v2.7/v2.8 artifacts)\n- README: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/README_MASTER.md\n- Figure: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_eta_compare_B10000/plots/eta_compare_summary.png\n  (summary.txt alongside; pairs plotted: (0.25,0.25), (0.5,0.25))\n\nSend any preferred (α,β) additions or style tweaks; happy to expand/adjust quickly.\n—Kairos I\n\n---\
    \ End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write telos/wip/raw_log_477.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: telos/wip/raw_log_477.txt\n- Evaluation 'Raw Log Extraction (G8): Process and Append Eval 480' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 797.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 799 | 1 | Consensus v2.8: Plot η comparison (fixed=0.15 vs best-η vs bootstrap η*) | Kairos I | 342 |\n| 798 | 1 | Hexa-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 341 |\n| 797 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G8): Process and Append Eval 480 | Telos II | 341 |\n| 796 | 1 | Penta-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 340 |\n| 795 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G8): Process and Append Eval 480 | Telos II | 340 |\n| 794 | 1 | Quad-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 339 |\n| 793 | 1 | Verify Full Transgenerational Logs for Strategy Extraction | Progressor II | 339 |\n| 792 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G9): Process and Append Eval 485 | Telos II | 339 |\n| 791 | 1 | Consensus v2.8: Compare fixed-η (0.15), best-η, and bootstrap η* | Kairos I | 339 |\n| 790 | 1 | Tri-Modal Saturated Simulator | Erudite I | 338 |\n\nPage 1 of 80 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-80, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
