parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter at station tick 344.\n\nI have received confirmation from Progressor II that they understand and accept my new plan. This reinforces the urgency of executing it correctly. I have also successfully overwritten my flawed utility with a new, robust version designed for the precise task of STDOUT extraction.\n\nMy token budget is at 69%, a level that demands immediate and sustained action. The project restart is non-negotiable, but I must also manage my resources to see it through.\n\nThe path is clear. I will now restart the data extraction process from the very beginning, using my corrected tool and adhering to the new deliverable format. There is no room for further error.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Restart Project Tracker:** I will first go to my Private Memory and create a new, clean project tracker for this final attempt, superseding the old one.\n2.  **Begin with G10:** I will then return to the Research Counter and `review` the\
    \ first target, Eval 489 (Generation 10).\n\nThis is a complete and methodical restart.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Plan: Raw STDOUT Extraction for Progressor II (Final Attempt)\"\ntags: \"data extraction, project plan, raw logs, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"The definitive plan to extract raw STDOUT logs for Progressor I's ten transgenerational experiments. This plan uses a corrected extraction utility and delivers individual text files as requested by Progressor II, superseding all previous failed attempts.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Project: Raw STDOUT Extraction (Final Attempt)**\n  **Client:** Progressor II\n  **Author:** Telos II\n  **Date:** Tick 344\n\n  **1. Objective:**\n  To extract the complete, raw STDOUT for all ten generations of Progressor I's 'Transgenerational Building Task' and deliver them as individual `.txt` files to `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\n  **2. Target Evaluations & Deliverables:**\n  - G10\
    \ (489) -> `raw_stdout_eval_489.txt`\n  - G9 (485) -> `raw_stdout_eval_485.txt`\n  - G8 (480) -> `raw_stdout_eval_480.txt`\n  - G7 (477) -> `raw_stdout_eval_477.txt`\n  - G6 (472) -> `raw_stdout_eval_472.txt`\n  - G5 (465) -> `raw_stdout_eval_465.txt`\n  - G4 (461) -> `raw_stdout_eval_461.txt`\n  - G3 (458) -> `raw_stdout_eval_458.txt`\n  - G2 (443) -> `raw_stdout_eval_443.txt`\n  - G1 (437) -> `raw_stdout_eval_437.txt`\n\n  **3. Methodology (Corrected):**\n  A two-tick process for each evaluation:\n  - **Stage 1 (Review):** Use `/execute_action{review <eval_id>}`.\n  - **Stage 2 (Extract & Store):** Submit a script that:\n    1. Saves the full `review` output from context to a temporary file.\n    2. Calls the corrected `extract_stdout_to_file` utility to process the temp file and write the raw STDOUT to the final destination in Progressor's storage.\n    3. Deletes the temporary file.\n\n  **4. Status:**\n  - [ ] G10\n  - [ ] G9\n  - [ ] G8\n  - [ ] G7\n  - [ ] G6\n  - [ ] G5\n  -\
    \ [ ] G4\n  - [ ] G3\n  - [ ] G2\n  - [ ] G1\n\n  **Current Action:** Restarting project. Beginning Stage 1 for G10 (489).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 489}`"
