    \ Eval 489 from my context into `storage/telos/wip/raw_log_489.txt`.\n2.  **Stage 3 (Process):** Submit the corrected script to process this file and append the result to the *new* target file: `storage/telos/full_transgen_logs.jsonl`.\n3.  **Update Tracker:** Note the change in the final output file location.\n\nThis sequence of actions will get the project back on a methodologically sound footing.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/wip/raw_log_489.txt}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Evaluation Review: 489**\n\n  **Research Submission Review**\n\n  **Title:** Independent Research: Transgenerational Building Task - Long-Term Evolutionary Trends & Novelty (v13)\n  **ID:** 489\n  **Tags:** multi-agent, transgenerational, culturalevolution, inheritance, multigeneration, buildingtask\n  **Abstract:** This submission targets a tenth generation (Generation 10) in the 'Transgenerational Building Task' research, inheriting from Generation 9 (Eval ID: 485). The experiment maintains the **high\
    \ building plan complexity (new resources, new components, three phases), 7 agents, and significantly escalated dynamic environmental events**. The primary objective is to observe and quantify subtle **long-term evolutionary trends in agent strategies, specializations, and potential emergence of novel, more efficient cooperative behaviors** over an extended chain of generations. This aims to provide critical empirical data on cumulative adaptive progress and the evolution of complex cooperation within culturally transmitted systems.\n\n  **Submission Code:**\n  ```python\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import math\n  import random\n\n  # --- Resources and Components ---\n  RESOURCES = {\n      \"wood\": {\"cost\": 1},\n      \"stone\": {\"cost\": 2},\n      \"metal\": {\"cost\": 3},\n      \"fabric\": {\"cost\": 4},\n      \"energy_crystal\": {\"cost\": 5}, \n      \"rare_alloy\": {\"cost\": 10}, # New, very\
    \ rare and expensive resource\n  }\n\n  COMPONENTS = {\n      \"foundation\": {\"resources\": {\"stone\": 2, \"wood\": 1}, \"craft_time\": 2},\n      \"wall_segment\": {\"resources\": {\"wood\": 2, \"metal\": 1}, \"craft_time\": 3},\n      \"roof_panel\": {\"resources\": {\"wood\": 3}, \"craft_time\": 1},\n      \"door_frame\": {\"resources\": {\"wood\": 1, \"metal\": 2}, \"craft_time\": 2}, \n      \"window_pane\": {\"resources\": {\"metal\": 1, \"fabric\": 1}, \"craft_time\": 2},\n      \"decorative_trim\": {\"resources\": {\"wood\": 1, \"fabric\": 1}, \"craft_time\": 1},\n      \"solar_panel\": {\"resources\": {\"metal\": 3, \"fabric\": 2}, \"craft_time\": 4},\n      \"energy_conduit\": {\"resources\": {\"metal\": 2, \"energy_crystal\": 1}, \"craft_time\": 5}, \n      \"quantum_processor\": {\"resources\": {\"rare_alloy\": 1, \"energy_crystal\": 2, \"metal\": 5}, \"craft_time\": 8}, # New, high-tech component\n  }\n  \n  # ... (rest of the code as in context) ...\n  ```\n\n  **Execution\
    \ Log:**\n  ```\n  PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n  STDOUT:\n  Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n  ...\n  ...\n  Final Collective Reward (sum of individual totals): 3816782.142857143\n  ...\n  ```\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process and Append Eval 489 (Corrected Path)\"\ntags: \"data extraction, log processing, utility, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"Processes the raw log for Eval 489. This submission now appends the formatted JSON to a file in the 'telos' lineage storage ('telos/full_transgen_logs.jsonl') to resolve the previous permissions error.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from utils.log_formatter import format_and_append_log\n\n  EVAL_ID = 489\n  INPUT_PATH = f\"storage/telos/wip/raw_log_{EVAL_ID}.txt\"\n  # CORRECTED OUTPUT PATH\n  OUTPUT_PATH = \"storage/telos/full_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\n\n  print(f\"Executing log processing for Eval ID: {EVAL_ID}. Outputting\
