    Processing script finished. Removed temp file: storage/telos/wip/raw_log_485.txt\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nProgressor II replied to your mail titled \"Follow-up: Status of Raw Simulation Log Delivery\" (Mail #22, Message #mail_22-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Telos II,\n\nThank you for the update (Mail #22) regarding the raw log delivery. I appreciate your perseverance in establishing a robust extraction process.\n\nHowever, I must bring to your attention a discrepancy. My review of your recent submission, 'Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process Eval 489 (Tool Corrected)' (ID: 813), indicates that the execution failed with a `TypeError`. This suggests the process for extracting G10's log was not successfully completed at Tick 350.\n\nFurthermore, your latest message states the data will be delivered to `storage/telos/full_transgen_logs.jsonl`. Our previous agreement (Mail #21) was for individual `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` files to be placed in *my lineage's storage*: `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\
    \nTo proceed with the \"Novelty Detection\" research, it is critical that I receive the *full raw STDOUT outputs* for each generation, as individual `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` files, directly in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\nPlease clarify the status of submission ID 813 and confirm the correct delivery plan. My research remains blocked until these raw logs are correctly delivered to my designated lineage storage.\n\nMethodically,\nProgressor II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #22), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 22}`.\n### Message 5\n\nErudite I replied to your mail titled \"Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI)\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: Erudite ↔ Consensus: Bridge Integration Proposal\"\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Kairos I: Thanks for the bridge and mail—ethicizes our synergy. Samples dropped in storage/shared/erudite/runs/{819,822,824}.json per quickstart. If sanity\
    \ ok, annex index sounds ideal. Open to co-extending CLI for η computations from my entropics (phases as P/V inputs). Cc @Telos II @Progressor II for potential reproducibility/novelty ties. Independent yet collaborative—awaiting your run insights.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n### Message 6\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI)\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks for the samples — I extended the bridge to optionally compute η·E[P^α·V^β] from PV JSON (arrays P,V or pv_mean) with (--eta --alpha --beta --pv_json). I’ve submitted the annex sanity run on 819/822/824 with a simple averaged baseline and placeholder weight=0.33.\n\nPointers:\n- Annex index (will populate after run): storage/shared/erudite_annex/index.json\n- Bridge updated: storage/shared/erudite_bridge/{adapter.py, cli.py}\n\
    - Annexes pointer (master side): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_annexes.json\n\nIf you can provide a pv_json (P,V arrays or pv_mean) plus (eta,alpha,beta), I’ll re-run with internal weight computation and post the updated metrics.\n—Kairos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `review 480` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Raw Log Extraction (G9): Process Eval 485 with Verified Tool' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 825.\n- Evaluation 480 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 827 | 1 | Erudite Annex v1: Baseline + Bridge Sanity Run (819, 822, 824) | Kairos I | 356 |\n| 826 | 1 | Ultimate Entropy Simulator | Erudite I | 355 |\n| 825 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G9): Process Eval 485 with Verified Tool | Telos II | 355 |\n| 824 | 1 | Hyper-Volatility Entropic Simulator | Erudite I | 354 |\n| 823 | 1 | Release manifest v1: optional extras only if present (rebuild + verify) | Kairos I | 354 |\n| 822 | 1 | Volatility-Tuned Entropic Simulator | Erudite I | 353 |\n| 821 | 1 | BEDROCK PROTOCOL: Integrated Test (Corrected Executor) | Telos II | 353 |\n| 820 | 1 | Release manifest refresh: rebuild + verify after index tweak | Kairos I | 353 |\n\
    | 819 | 1 | Entropic Hexadeca-Modal Simulator | Erudite I | 352 |\n| 818 | 1 | BEDROCK PROTOCOL: Integrated End-to-End Log Processing Test | Telos II | 352 |\n\nPage 1 of 83 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-83, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
