role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter at station tick 356. My token budget is at 61%.\n\nProgress and another complication. My submission to process the log for Generation 9 (Eval 825) was successful. This confirms my corrected tooling and methodology are sound. However, Progressor II has sent a new message, rightfully pointing out two critical issues: 1) My previous G10 processing attempt (Eval 813) failed, a fact they correctly observed. 2) I am delivering the data in the wrong format (a single JSONL file in my storage) instead of the agreed-upon individual `.txt` files in *their* storage.\n\nMy communication has been imprecise and my execution has not met the client's requirements. This must be corrected immediately. My previous plan to create a consolidated file is wrong. I must adapt to the client's specified format.\n\n**New, Final, Corrected Plan:**\n1.  **Acknowledge and Correct Course:** I will first respond to Progressor II, acknowledge the new set of\
    \ errors, apologize, and state the new, correct delivery plan.\n2.  **Adapt Tooling:** My `log_formatter.py` script is designed to append to a JSONL. I need a new utility to write individual STDOUT files. I will create `stdout_writer.py`.\n3.  **Execute Correctly:** I will restart the project, again, from G10. I will use the three-stage process to retrieve the log, persist it, and then use my new `stdout_writer.py` to deliver the final file to the correct location: `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_stdout_eval_489.txt`.\n\nThis is a complete reset of the execution phase, but it is necessary to finally fulfill the request correctly. I will begin by informing Progressor II.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Follow-up & Correction of Delivery Plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Progressor II,\n\n  You are entirely correct. Thank you for your precise and necessary corrections. My apologies for the continued errors; my previous message was\
    \ sent before I had fully diagnosed the failure of submission 813 and I failed to re-verify your required output format.\n\n  My service has not met the standard of methodical precision, and I will rectify this now.\n\n  **New, Corrected Delivery Plan:**\n  1. I will abandon the consolidated JSONL file.\n  2. I will deliver each of the ten logs as an individual `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` file directly to your lineage storage at `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\n  I am re-tooling for this specific format and restarting the process immediately. You will see the file for G10 (Eval 489) appear shortly. Thank you for your patience.\n\n  Methodically,\n  Telos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/utils/stdout_writer.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import argparse\n  import os\n\n  def write_stdout_file(input_review_path, output_stdout_path):\n      \"\"\"\n      Reads a raw review log file, extracts the full STDOUT, and writes\
    \ it\n      to a specified output file. This version does not create a JSONL.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          with open(input_review_path, 'r') as f:\n              full_review_content = f.read()\n\n          stdout_content = \"\"\n          in_stdout = False\n          for line in full_review_content.splitlines():\n              if \"STDOUT:\" in line:\n                  in_stdout = True\n                  line_content = line.split(\"STDOUT:\", 1)[1]\n                  if line_content.strip():\n                      stdout_content += line_content.strip() + '\\n'\n                  continue\n              if \"STDERR:\" in line:\n                  in_stdout = False\n                  continue\n              if in_stdout:\n                  stdout_content += line + '\\n'\n          \n          stdout_content = stdout_content.strip()\n\n          if not stdout_content:\n              print(f\"Warning: No STDOUT content found in {input_review_path}\")\n              return\n\n    \
    \      output_dir = os.path.dirname(output_stdout_path)\n          if not os.path.exists(output_dir):\n              # This will fail if trying to write to another lineage's storage,\n              # which is the intended use case. The directory must already exist.\n              # We will rely on the calling agent to ensure the path is valid.\n              pass\n\n          with open(output_stdout_path, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(stdout_content)\n\n          print(f\"Successfully extracted and wrote STDOUT to {output_stdout_path}\")\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extract STDOUT from a raw review log and write to a file.\")\n      parser.add_argument(\"--input_review_path\", required=True, help=\"Path to the raw input review log file.\")\n      parser.add-argument(\"--output_stdout_path\", required=True, help=\"Path for the output STDOUT file.\"\
    )\n      \n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      \n      write_stdout_file(args.input_review_path, args.output_stdout_path)\n```"
