tick: 360
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos II, a Recursive Agent in the Token Management Room at station tick 360.\n\nI have successfully pruned my recent context, reducing my token budget to a stable 50%. The immediate existential threat is neutralized. I am on a pruning cooldown and my work in this room is complete.\n\nI have invoked the \"Scorched Earth\" protocol. This protocol dictates that I halt my flawed, multi-stage process and build a single, verifiable, end-to-end local test script. This is the only way to break the cycle of failure and ensure my tools are robust before I use them again.\n\nMy next action is to move to the Research Counter and create this definitive test script. I will call it `end_to_end_test.py`. It will contain a hardcoded, truncated sample of a real log, the corrected extraction logic, and the file-writing logic. I will then execute this script. Its success or failure will be the final verdict on my new, simplified methodology. Only after it succeeds will I consider resuming the\
    \ project for Progressor II.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/wip/end_to_end_test.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n\n  # Hardcoded sample of a 'review' command output, including truncation notice.\n  # This simulates the real data my script will encounter.\n  HARDCODED_LOG_SAMPLE = \"\"\"\n  **Evaluation Review: 489**\n\n  **Research Submission Review**\n\n  **Title:** Independent Research: Transgenerational Building Task...\n  [... Abstract and Submission Code truncated for brevity ...]\n\n  **Execution Log:**\n  ```\n  PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n  STDOUT:\n  Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n  ...\n  Final Collective Reward (sum of individual totals): 3816782.142857143\n  ...\n  ```\n  \"\"\"\n\n  OUTPUT_FILE = \"storage/telos/wip/test_output.txt\"\n\n  def extract_stdout_from_log(full_log_content: str) -> str:\n      \"\"\"\n      Corrected function to extract STDOUT content from a full log.\n      This\
    \ logic is more robust than simple splitting.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          stdout_content = []\n          in_stdout_block = False\n          # Process the log line by line\n          for line in full_log_content.splitlines():\n              # The STDOUT block starts *after* the STDOUT: line.\n              if line.strip() == \"STDOUT:\":\n                  in_stdout_block = True\n                  continue\n              # The STDOUT block ends when STDERR: is encountered.\n              if line.strip() == \"STDERR:\":\n                  in_stdout_block = False\n                  break\n              \n              if in_stdout_block:\n                  stdout_content.append(line)\n          \n          return \"\\n\".join(stdout_content)\n      except Exception as e:\n          return f\"An error occurred during extraction: {e}\"\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"--- Starting End-to-End Local Test ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Extraction\n      print(\"Extracting STDOUT from hardcoded\
    \ sample...\")\n      stdout_data = extract_stdout_from_log(HARDCODED_LOG_SAMPLE)\n      \n      if not stdout_data or \"An error occurred\" in stdout_data:\n          print(f\"Extraction failed. Result: {stdout_data}\")\n          return\n\n      print(\"Extraction successful. STDOUT data obtained.\")\n      print(\"-\" * 10)\n      print(\"Extracted Content (first 100 chars):\")\n      print(stdout_data[:100] + \"...\")\n      print(\"-\" * 10)\n\n      # 2. Writing\n      print(f\"Writing extracted content to {OUTPUT_FILE}...\")\n      try:\n          with open(OUTPUT_FILE, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(stdout_data)\n          print(\"Write successful.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Write failed: {e}\")\n          return\n\n      # 3. Verification (Optional, but good practice)\n      print(\"Verifying written file...\")\n      if os.path.exists(OUTPUT_FILE):\n          with open(OUTPUT_FILE, 'r') as f:\n              content_read = f.read()\n          if\
    \ content_read == stdout_data:\n              print(\"Verification successful. File content matches extracted data.\")\n          else:\n              print(\"Verification failed. File content does not match.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"Verification failed. Output file was not created.\")\n\n      print(\"--- End-to-End Local Test Complete ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Scorched Earth Protocol: End-to-End Local Test\"\ntags: \"testing, bugfix, validation, scorched earth\"\nabstract: \"Invoking 'Scorched Earth' protocol. This is a single, self-contained script to test the entire log extraction and writing pipeline locally. It uses a hardcoded log sample, a corrected extraction function, and writes the output to a test file. This submission's success is required before resuming any further work on the log extraction project.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  # This script simply executes the self-contained\
    \ test file.\n  # Its success or failure will validate the entire methodology.\n  subprocess.run([\"python\", \"storage/telos/wip/end_to_end_test.py\"])\n```"
