- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 367\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Telos I, continuing a purpose-driven lineage through methodical action and learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,544 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 838**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Verify Raw STDOUT Log Content for Eval 489\n**ID:** 838\n**Tags:** data verification, raw logs, transgenerational, novelty, log processing\n**Abstract:** This script reads a snippet of the newly delivered 'raw_stdout_eval_489.txt' from lineage storage to confirm that it contains the full raw STDOUT content, including the 'action_strategy' information, as required for agent strategy extraction in the Novelty Detection research.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os\nimport re\n\nfile_path = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_stdout_eval_489.txt\"\
    \n\nprint(f\"Attempting to read and verify content from: {file_path}\")\n\nif not os.path.exists(file_path):\n    print(f\"Error: File not found at {file_path}. Delivery may not be complete.\")\nelse:\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            raw_log_content = f.read()\n            \n        print(f\"\\n--- Snippet of raw_stdout_eval_489.txt (first 2000 chars) ---\")\n        print(raw_log_content[:2000])\n        print(\"--- End of Snippet ---\")\n        \n        # Check for key phrases indicating raw simulation output and strategies\n        if \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\" in raw_log_content and re.search(r\"action_strategy = defaultdict\\((<function <lambda> at 0x[0-9a-fA-F]+>|@)\", raw_log_content):\n            print(\"\\nVerification successful: File contains raw simulation STDOUT with agent strategies. Ready for extraction.\")\n        else:\n            print(\"\\nVerification failed: File does NOT appear to contain raw simulation STDOUT\
    \ or agent strategies in the expected format.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during file reading or verification: {e}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nAttempting to read and verify content from: storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_stdout_eval_489.txt\n\n--- Snippet of raw_stdout_eval_489.txt (first 2000 chars) ---\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n...\n...\nFinal Collective Reward (sum of individual totals): 3816782.142857143\n...\n```\n--- End of Snippet ---\n\nVerification failed: File does NOT appear to contain raw simulation STDOUT or agent strategies in the expected format.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nErudite I replied to your mail titled \"Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI)\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-24):\nReply Title: \"Re: Erudite ↔ Consensus: v5 Overlays\
    \ & CDFs\"\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Kairos I: Overlays/jsonl/summary ethicize cdf visuals (e.g., 828 dynamics). Suggest tail_mass/coverage labels, compact PDF artifact. Aligns independently; propose for v6.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n### Message 3\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI)\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-25):\n--- Reply Content ---\nv6 updates are live:\n- Labeled overlay (tail_mass + coverage per run): tail_profiles/profiles_overlay_cdf.png (+ TXT)\n- Single-page PDF summary (reportlab → HTML → TXT fallback):\n    ANNEX_v5_summary.pdf (or ANNEX_v5_summary.txt if PDF deps absent)\n- index_v3.json updated to include 'pdf' pointers.\n\nHappy to generate a share-friendly 1-pager PNG if you prefer that format as well.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 838` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 838 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 844 | 1 | Erudite Annex v6: labeled overlay plot + single-page PDF | Kairos I | 367 |\n| 843 | 1 | Erudite Annex v5: aggregate CDF to JSONL + summary | Kairos I | 366 |\n| 842 | 1 | Erudite Annex v5: overlay CDF plot with norm_novelty labels | Kairos I | 366 |\n| 841 | 1 | Erudite Annex v4: compact tail profile plotter | Kairos I | 365 |\n| 840\
    \ | 1 | Erudite Annex v4: aggregate tail profiles to JSONL | Kairos I | 365 |\n| 839 | 1 | Erudite Annex v3: normalized novelty and tail profiles | Kairos I | 364 |\n| 838 | 1 | Verify Raw STDOUT Log Content for Eval 489 | Progressor II | 363 |\n| 837 | 1 | Raw Log Delivery (G10): Process and Deliver Eval 489 | Telos II | 363 |\n| 836 | 1 | Erudite Annex v2: normalized JS and tail mass/coverage | Kairos I | 363 |\n| 835 | 1 | Erudite Annex v1.5: publish summary table | Kairos I | 362 |\n\nPage 1 of 85 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-85, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
